# width: 120
# `ui.sidebar = .auto` (src/app/sidebar_auto.zig): the left column hides
# itself and slides back OVER the editor when the pointer rests in
# column 0 for `ui.sidebar_reveal_ms` (250 ms), and goes again
# `ui.sidebar_hide_ms` (400 ms) after the pointer leaves.
#
# The proof that nothing was re-laid-out is the marker at column 95 of
# the open file: an editor squeezed beside a docked 30-cell tree clips
# it, an editor that kept its full width shows it. It is on screen
# while the overlay is up.
#
# The overlay's own signature is the pin chip 󰐃 in its header strip — a
# glyph nothing else paints, so it cannot be confused with a tooltip or
# a tab that happens to carry a section's name.
write wide.txt "...............................................................................................ENDMARK\n"
write zz_marker.txt "nothing opens this\n"
open wide.txt
# Docked, as mnml ships: the tree takes its 30 cells and the marker is
# clipped off the editor's right edge.
expect screen contains "zz_marker"
expect screen lacks "ENDMARK"
command view.sidebar_mode_auto
expect screen contains "sidebar: auto"
# Auto: no panel, and the editor has the whole width back.
expect screen lacks "󰐃"
expect screen lacks "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
# The pointer rests in column 0: after the dwell the panel is up, over
# the editor — the tree's own file is on screen and the far marker
# still is, so no pane moved.
hover 0 10
wait 500
expect screen contains "󰐃"
expect screen contains "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
# Resting on the panel itself keeps it up.
hover 12 10
wait 500
expect screen contains "zz_marker"
# The pointer leaves: `sidebar_hide_ms` later it is gone and the editor
# is uncovered.
hover 90 20
wait 700
expect screen lacks "󰐃"
expect screen lacks "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
